Policies have to be able to do something.

We can construct abstract policies which should be basically cross-platform as the principal/action/resource thing is fairly standard.
However, we are going to sail closer to the AWS wind because that's our target.
I don't think I'm going to over-commit, but you never know.

This example is just a really simple one that we can create a policy.
Note that this is entirely in memory: you need to "ensure" it somewhere or attach it to something to make it take shape in the real world.

	target createAPolicyAllowingOneThing
		policy => allow_one_policy
			allow "action" "resource"
		